"The RX 6000 has neither FP8 nor matrix units, so this runs the RX 7000's FP16\nnetwork with its matrices worked out in ordinary FP16 dot products: much slower\nthan on an RX 9000 or RX 7000, and about 2 GB more VRAM at 1080p. Every pipeline\nwas compiled once apart from the game before the first build.\nExperimental: if the picture looks wrong or the game stutters, turn NR off and report it.",
"The RX 7000 has no FP8, so this runs mauri870's port of the network to FP16\nmatrices: slower than on an RX 9000, and about 2 GB more VRAM at 1080p. The GPU's\nmatrix layout and every pipeline were checked before the first build.\nExperimental: if the picture looks wrong, turn NR off and report it.",
"The Way It's Meant To Be Upscaled",
"The best input the game sends: Reflex, XeLL when enabled in the game, AntiLag 2, UE, XeLL.\nAntiLag 2 first while the game's FSR-FG reports its frames through it.\nWithout any, OptiScaler's own with the DLSSG output.",
