"The model is handed the render-resolution frame the upscaler is about to\nread, so the percentage below is of that render resolution. The upscaler\nthen enlarges the model\'s work along with everything else.",
"The model was trained on finished, sRGB-encoded frames. The upscaler's\noutput is not one: it is linear and open-ended. These decide how it is\nmapped into something the model recognises. A frame the game reports as\nalready tone-mapped is passed over untouched and none of this applies.",
"The model's own processing profiles. Standard is NVIDIA's default; Natural is\nthe one lmxxf's kernels had built in before. Changing it rebuilds the model,\na pause of a second or two.",
"The more you upscaler, the more you save",
"The most the composition may brighten or darken a pixel, as a multiple of what it was.\nOne number from the brightness, applied to the whole colour, so it bounds light without\ntouching hue. 2.0x by default; raise it only if bright areas look held back.",
"The most the pass may move any pixel, as a multiple of what it already was, in\nboth directions -- a pixel may not be brightened past this nor darkened past\nits reciprocal. Lights are where the model has least to say and rescaling its\nanswer does the most damage; 2x leaves detail intact while stopping a strip\nlight turning into a string of coloured cells. Raise it only if bright areas\nlook clipped.",
"The network NR runs, by its name in NVIDIA's DLL, as mochizuki's NR Control lists them.\nCC_SMALL_FP8: the model of 310.9.16, the default and fastest.\nCC_SMALL_FP8_EXPERIMENTAL: that model made faster by mochizuki; its picture differs somewhat.\nCC_SILVER_AARDWOLD: the model of 310.8.\nCC_SILVER_AARDWOLD_OPTIMIZED: the 310.8 model made faster by mochizuki, its picture very close.\nThe two faster ones need ACO on an RX 9000; their weights are made from the installed model the\nfirst time. Switching builds the other network in a few seconds while the current one keeps\nrunning; no restart.",
"The network also reads its own result from the previous frame, moved along the\ngame's motion vectors. Keeps the effect steadier in motion. Off runs every frame\non its own.",
"The network runs on a smaller copy of the frame: full resolution in the centre, lower toward\nthe edges, and its change is put back on the full frame, so the game's own detail stays\neverywhere and only the effect gets softer at the sides. NR pixels at 16:9: about 80% light,\n70% medium, 45-50% strong. Each change rebuilds the network and restarts its history.\nBefore the upscaler it runs with mochizuki only (the render frame is warped, the upscaler\nkeeps its jitter); off while person protection runs.\nCustom takes FoveationCentreWidth/Height, FoveationFalloff and FoveationEdge from the INI.",
"The network's history in RGBA16F, as NVIDIA's DLL keeps it (half the memory). Off keeps\nRGBA32F, the picture before. An RX 9000 with ACO off keeps 32-bit. Rebuilds the network.",
